#X text 30 900 Arguments: which held key sounds (0 the last pressed - 1 the lowest - 2 the highest) and legato (1 on). Takes the keys as pitch - velocity. Sends one note at a time as pitch - velocity - legato: the chosen key when the choice changes. When its key is let go it goes back to another held key. and off when none is. Legato is 1 for a note that follows another with no key up between. when legato is on.;
